<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch March CPI seen at 2.1 pct y/y. [CORRECTED 14:38 GMT]</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch March CPI seen at 2.1 pct y/y. [CORRECTED 14:38 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline from &quot;CPI seen rising 2.1 pct&quot;)</p>
<p>Dutch economists forecast Dutch March consumer price inflation would fall to a year-on-year rate of 2.1 percent from 2.2 (Corrects from 1.6) percent in February.</p>
<p>The March consumer inflation data is due to be published at 0830 GMT on Monday. Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT--Date---Period-Indicator---------Consensus--Range------Pvs</p>
<p> 0830 07/04  March  CPI Mth/Mth	 0.7 pct    0.5/0.9    0.2</p>
<p> 0830 07/04  March  CPI Yr/Yr	   2.1 pct    1.9/2.3    2.2 (Corrects from 1.6)</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, NIBStrating, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
